Package: audiobookshelf
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: systemd, ffmpeg
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.audiobookshelf.org
Description: Self-hosted audiobook and podcast server for TOS
 Audiobookshelf is a self-hosted server for managing and playing
 your audiobooks and podcasts. It ships the upstream
 single-executable build (Node.js runtime with the web client
 embedded); media processing and transcoding use the ffmpeg/
 ffprobe from the TOS base system (declared via Depends).
 .
 The web UI opens in a new browser tab via the TOS App Center route
 /audiobookshelf/. The backend listens on loopback only; no external
 port is exposed. Data (config, library database, metadata, backups)
 is stored under /var/lib/audiobookshelf. Library folders on TOS
 shares must be granted to the app user via shared-folder
 permissions.
 Upstream author: advplyr (https://github.com/advplyr/audiobookshelf)
 Packaged for TOS by Moechz
